2ce0918dfbff8b"],"findings":"I found five suggestions. They come from reading the diff only: I didn't apply them or run the tests, so each one is marked **read**.\n\n1. **Share one pattern normaliser in `src/config.ts` (h17).** **read**\n   - The `Regex` schema's `superRefine` and `compile` each derive `source` and `flags` from a `RawPattern` with the same ternaries (`typeof p === 'string' ? … : …`, default flag `'i'`). The default flag is written in both places.\n   - A single `normalize(p): { source, flags, name }` would be used by both. The schema would call `new RegExp` on the result, and `compile` would add `re`.\n   - The default flag would then live in one place and could not drift between validation and use.\n   - Size: about 10 lines.\n\n2. **Compute a hunk's floor in one place (group `signals-engine`, `src/signals.ts`).** **read**\n   - `hunkSignals` builds `floor` and `why` from path floor plus live hits. `partFloor` repeats the same logic for a subset of lines (the `live` filter, `maxImpact` fold, `pattern:` names, and the `startsWith('pattern:')` filtering of reasons).\n   - Both could call one helper `floorFrom(pathFloor, pathWhy, hits, lines | null)`, so `hunkSignals` would just be `floorFrom(..., null)`.\n   - The two copies already differ slightly: `hunkSignals` de-duplicates with `includes`, while `partFloor` uses a `Set`. That is how a fix ends up applied to only one of them.\n   - Size: about 15 lines removed.\n   - The related `damped` and `inert` computations (the repeated `classes.includes('test') || …` chains) could each be a small `has(...)` over a list.\n\n3. **Reuse `attentionRank` in `src/render.ts` (group `show-display`).** **read**\n   - `belowFloor` does `ATTENTION.indexOf(a.level) < ATTENTION.indexOf(view.floor)`, which is exactly `attentionRank` from `signals.ts`.\n   - `floor.ts` and `html/data.ts` already import from `signals.ts`. Importing it here drops the new `ATTENTION` import in `render.ts` and keeps the comparison in one place.\n   - Moving `attentionRank`, `maxAttention`, `raise` and `attentionForImpact` into `attention.ts`, next to `impactRank`, would also avoid `render.ts` depending on the signals engine. `attention.ts` is where the existing rank helper already lives.\n   - Size: a few lines.\n\n4. **Share the \"signals unavailable\" fallback between `hunks.ts` and `floor.ts` (groups `hunks-summary` and `floor-derive`).** **read**\n   - `hunks.ts` has its own `try/catch (ConfigError)` that prints `warning: signals unavailable: …`. `tryAnalyze` in `floor.ts` does the same, but it also adds a `warned` flag so the message prints once.\n   - Extract `withSignals<T>(fn: () => T): T | null` in `config.ts` or `floor.ts`, with the warn-once behaviour, and use it in both. `hunks` would become `const sig = withSignals(() => analyze(hunks, loadConfig()))`.\n   - Size: about 10 lines.\n\n5. **Tidy `test/signals.test.ts` (group `signals-tests`).** **read**\n   - Delete the dead `const base = … ; void base`.\n   - Replace `execFileSync('cat', [out])` with `readFileSync(out, 'utf8')`, which also avoids spawning a process.\n   - The HTML-data extraction is copy-pasted in two tests. A small `pageData(path)` helper would cover both.\n   - Size: about 8 lines.\n\nThe change is otherwise reasonably lean. There is no unnecessary abstraction, and the glob matcher is justified by the Node 20 gap.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
