ce0918dfbff8b"],"findings":"I applied the first two suggestions in the clone and ran the full suite: 166 pass, 0 fail, and `tsc --noEmit` is clean. The rest are from reading the code only.\n\n**1. Drop the speculative `reserved-config-keys` group** (`src/config.ts`, group `reserved-config-keys`) — **verified**\n`manyProjects` and `impactCommand` are accepted by the schema but nothing reads them. `manyProjects` is still in the `loadConfig` loop, so `git config gloss.attention.manyProjects` is read and then ignored. Removing both keys and making the loop a single key drops about 6 lines and removes config that silently does nothing. The cost is that a config written for a later version now fails validation. That is acceptable while the feature is unreleased. Applied: tsc and 166/166 tests pass.\n\n**2. Remove the unused `matchAny`** (`src/glob.ts:58`) — **verified**\nOnly its own definition references it. The deletion is one line, and tests still pass. Applied.\n\n**3. Compute the hunk floor once, through `partFloor`** (`src/signals.ts`, `hunkSignals` and `partFloor`) — **read**\n`hunkSignals` repeats the logic of `partFloor` (path floor, then undamped hits, then the `why` filtering). `partFloor(s, null)` gives the same floor and reasons. Having `hunkSignals` call that path, or sharing one helper, removes a second copy of the rule. This is about 10 lines. I did not apply it, so I have not run the tests.\n\n**4. Share the two group-input builders** (`src/floor.ts`, `groupInputs` and `groupInputsFor`) — **read**\nBoth return `{ group, parts: {hunk, lines}[] }`, and they differ only in where the hunks and line sets come from. A single function taking the hunk list and a selection map would remove one function. The benefit is small.\n\n**5. Avoid a `git` spawn per call in `loadConfig`** (`src/config.ts`, `loadConfig`) — **read**\n`loadConfig` runs `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` on every call before it checks the cache. `html` calls `tryAnalyze` once per commit, so that is one extra process per commit. Caching by `process.cwd()`, or only checking the cache after the first call, would avoid it. It only matters for large `html` renders, so it is low priority.\n\nAlso minor: `derivedImpactTag` in `src/render.ts` could be `impactTag` with a dim flag, and `derivedBadge` in `src/html/client.js` duplicates `levelBadge`. I did not count these among the five.\n\nThe clone has the two edits applied (`src/config.ts`, `src/glob.ts`) and nothing committed. Under the repo's CLAUDE.md, the author's real working tree would need a wip-gloss if these edits were carried over; I did not run that here.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES\n\nThe waiter I started earlier (`brlj013uw`) was stopped at its time limit. It was only polling, so nothing was lost. The test result comes from the separate run (`bo0pee71t`), which finished with exit 0: 166 tests, 166 pass, 0 fail, after the two edits in `src/config.ts` and `src/glob.ts`. My earlier report stands. The edits are still uncommitted in the clone.","verdict":"issues"}
